From: DANOS <noreply@danos.io>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:00:00 +0800
Subject: meson: fall back to a manual libtirpc probe if pkg-config misses it

Debian's own Revert-m4-virt-xdr-rewrite-XDR-check.patch used to force
xdr_dep to an empty declare_dependency() on Linux, working around a
glibc 2.31 bug where headers came from libtirpc but symbols resolved
against glibc's own (then still present) obsolete Sun RPC compat
symbols, producing bad linking. That revert is now dropped: current
glibc (2.41 here) has removed rpc/rpc.h and the obsolete RPC symbols
entirely, so the double-linking risk the revert guarded against no
longer exists, and Debian:13/standard's build root fails outright on
`#include <rpc/rpc.h>` without libtirpc.

dependency('libtirpc', required: false) should find libtirpc-dev's
pkg-config file. If it does not, for whatever reason, try a direct
header/library probe before giving up, since libtirpc's non-standard
include prefix (/usr/include/tirpc) is the one thing a bare pkg-config
miss cannot recover from on its own -- this keeps the failure at
configure time (a clear message) instead of a much more confusing
compile-time failure deep inside generated RPC code.
---
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1431,6 +1431,15 @@
   xdr_dep = cc.find_library('portablexdr', required: false)
 elif host_machine.system() == 'linux'
   xdr_dep = dependency('libtirpc', required: false)
+  if not xdr_dep.found()
+    tirpc_lib = cc.find_library('tirpc', required: false)
+    if tirpc_lib.found() and cc.has_header('rpc/rpc.h', args: '-I/usr/include/tirpc')
+      xdr_dep = declare_dependency(
+        dependencies: tirpc_lib,
+        include_directories: include_directories('/usr/include/tirpc'),
+      )
+    endif
+  endif
 else
   xdr_dep = declare_dependency()
 endif
